{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"The level-1 control experiment rules out path history: detours and early rotations still win at the same final pose. That sharpens the model—reward depends on exact socket geometry, not merely visiting pegs. The earlier “bridge” tests were too permissive, so I’m identifying which peg pairs match each body’s actual connector orientation before searching relay sequences."}}
